WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.790
After becoming so invested in the story and
characters, it's hard to move on from Game

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:05.420
of Thrones.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:10.240
But the producers, writers, and actors behind
the series have left Westeros behind for new

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.560
projects, and it looks like there's no going
back.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.060
Here's why you shouldn't expect a Game of
Thrones sequel anytime soon.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.960
Ready for a season nine of Game of Thrones?

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:19.460
What about a tenth?

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.340
HBO President of Programming Casey Bloys is
on record as having been willing to back many

00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:26.060
more seasons of the smash hit series.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.009
But instead of forcing the show to continue
indefinitely, he allowed the creative team

00:00:30.009 --> 00:00:32.560
to make the ultimate decision regarding when
it would end.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:36.980
Apparently, showrunners David Benioff and
D.B. Weiss knew how they wanted the ending

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:41.000
to go for a long time, and Bloys let them
wrap things up on their terms.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.340
And that ending, it seems, is pretty definitive.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.440
When asked about potential sequel series that
may be in the works, Bloys told The Hollywood

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:47.940
Reporter:

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.140
"Nope, nope, nope.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:49.860
No.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.500
Part of it is, I do want this show...to be
its own thing.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.100
I don't want to take characters from this
world that they did beautifully and put them

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.539
off into another world with someone else creating
it."

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.540
In other words, don't hold out hope for that
Arya Goes West spinoff.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.740
Author George R.R. Martin is supposed to be
working diligently on The Winds of Winter,

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:11.040
but he's also found time to publish several
books plotting out hundreds of years of Westerosi

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:11.540
history.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:15.800
There is a wealth of material set in the past,
and HBO has flirted with adapting more than

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.160
a few stories for television.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:21.680
"If we forget where we've been, what we've
done, we're not men anymore.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:23.720
We're just animals."

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:29.380
Of the possible projects, one prequel series
is definitely moving ahead with a pilot being

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:33.660
filmed and an announced cast list that includes
Naomi Watts and Josh Whitehouse.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:38.320
The as-yet unnamed prequel series will take
place thousands of years before the events

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:42.450
of Game of Thrones as it chronicles the world’s
descent from the golden Age of Heroes into

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.480
its darkest hour.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:47.080
There's little word on the other projects
in development, which may well never come

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:47.800
to fruition.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.520
But if one spinoff proves successful, chances
are more will follow.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.960
Further prequels could follow the events of
Martin's Fire &amp; Blood, which details how King

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:59.420
Aegon the Dragon conquered Westeros with his
royal sisters.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.660
Another prequel series could also adapt some
of the tales collected in the short story

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:08.040
volume A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms, which
follow a towering hedge knight named Duncan,

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:12.810
who's an ancestor of Brienne of Tarth, travelling
with and defending a little Targaryen prince

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.620
by the name of Aegon V, or simply "Egg."

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:20.620
There's still more material in Westeros' history
that seems perfect for television: the Blackfyre

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:24.120
Rebellions, the Targaryen civil war, the dark
tale of the Night's King.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:25.940
And that's just events from Westeros.

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:28.380
Essos has a long and storied history too.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.620
When it comes to stories set in the past,
Martin has given HBO quite a bit to work with.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:37.360
Game of Thrones viewers became accustomed
to the visual splendor of each episode over

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.720
the course of eight seasons.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:43.140
Each episode is like its own full-fledged
film, brought to life with reality-defying

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:47.870
special effects, lavish costuming, sets built
to scale, and massive casts of extras.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:51.740
As you might imagine, filming a season's worth
of small movies can get pretty expensive.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:56.190
The final season reportedly cost an estimated
$15 million per episode.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:03:00.740
It takes a lot of money to make dragons fly,
direwolves growl, and wights reanimate.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:06.000
HBO can afford to make entire series for $15
million rather than shelling out $15 million

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.120
for a single episode.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:12.160
Another Game of Thrones-scale series, especially
one that brought back the same increasingly-expensive

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.620
cast members, might be a bit too much of a
financial burden to be worth mounting.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.680
"It wasn't just about the money, was it?

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.840
Was it?…Was it?"

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:28.620
As the final credits roll on Game of Thrones,
a new era begins.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:33.580
High fantasy has proven itself to be extremely
profitable, so HBO and the BBC have teamed

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:38.320
up to make another fantasy show based on a
beloved book series: His Dark Materials.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:39.360
Political struggles?

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:39.860
Check.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:40.920
Mysterious powers?

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:41.580
Check.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:42.820
CGI animals?

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:43.400
Check.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:47.380
It isn't a Game of Thrones sequel, but it
may satisfy some of the same viewers who tuned

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:48.920
in to watch the fantasy unfold.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:53.459
Plus, if you're tired of fantasy lands, there
are plenty of other shows that HBO has cooking

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.940
that explore different genres.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:59.560
Westworld has another season on the way, for
those of the convoluted sci-fi loving persuasion.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:04.060
Fans of superheroes and contemplative graphic
novels can rejoice in the upcoming premiere

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.540
of the Watchmen adaptation.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:10.880
Jordan Peele and JJ Abrams are producing Lovecraft
Country, a horror drama that's almost guaranteed

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:11.500
to be a hit.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.940
Even now that we're done watching Thrones,
there are plenty of shows on the way that

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.020
will make your HBO subscription worth it.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.840
Even before the dust settled on Game of Thrones,
showrunners D.B. Weiss and David Benioff set

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.860
their sights on a galaxy far, far away.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:28.960
Disney CEO Bob Iger has confirmed that after
the twin suns set on the current trilogy of

00:04:28.979 --> 00:04:33.620
Star Wars films, Benioff and Weiss will be
working on the next series of films, a trilogy

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.580
telling a new story separate from the Skywalker
saga.

00:04:36.789 --> 00:04:41.400
The first of the three films is due at the
end of 2022, giving audiences plenty of time

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.920
to forget how upset they were at the final
Game of Thrones season.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.889
With two of the largest creative engines for
Game of Thrones headed to space, it doesn't

00:04:47.889 --> 00:04:51.260
seem like a Thrones sequel is in the cards,
at least not from them.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:54.660
Game of Thrones has changed television as
we know it.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:58.860
It's no longer satisfactory for shows to be
small with dedicated followings.

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:02.800
Every show wants to be a blockbuster, and
in the coming years, there will be no limit

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:06.520
to the number of titles seeking to fill the
void that the end of Game of Thrones has left

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:07.240
in our hearts.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.760
His Dark Materials isn't the only fantasy
adaptation on the table.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:14.819
Netflix is launching a series based on The
Witcher series of books, which has previously

00:05:14.819 --> 00:05:17.879
been adapted into a very successful video
game franchise.

00:05:17.879 --> 00:05:23.339
Amazon reportedly paid close to $250 million
for a Lord of the Rings prequel series.

00:05:23.339 --> 00:05:28.210
Meanwhile, Netflix is also planning a live-action
version of the beloved animated series Avatar:

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.120
The Last Airbender.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:33.699
Every major company is trying to replicate
the GoT success, and with a competition that

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:37.420
crowded, it's unlikely that a Game of Thrones
sequel would really stand out.

